 Ruby-Style-Leitfaden? Er ist ein Stilguide für Entwickler, der darauf abzielt, die Lesbarkeit und Konsistenz des Codes zu verbessern","pt":"O guia de estilo Ruby é um conjunto de regras para escrever código Ruby de forma clara e consistente","ru":"Руководство по стилю Ruby представляет собой набор правил для написания читаемого и последовательного кода Ruby","ar":"دليل أسلوب روبي هو مجموعة من القواعد لكتابة كود روبي بطريقة واضحة ومتناسقة"},"features":{"en":["Applies the official Ruby Style Guide for consistent coding","Based on RuboCop standards for automated code review","Enforces source code layout guidelines for better readability","Prioritizes consistency within a project over strict adherence to guidelines","Matches surrounding code when in doubt for seamless integration","Improves code maintainability and teamwork efficiency"],"zh":["基于 RuboCop 和 Ruby Style Guide","提高代码的可读性和一致性","社区驱动的风格指南","适用于 Ruby 代码的开发和审查","支持代码的格式化和优化"],"ja":["RuboCop と Ruby Style Guide に基づく","コードの可読性と一致性を高める","コミュニティ主導のスタイルガイド","Ruby コードの開発とレビューに適する","コードのフォーマットと最適化をサポート"],"ko":["RuboCop 및 Ruby Style Guide 기반","코드의 가독성과 일관성을 높인다","커뮤니티 주도 스타일 가이드","Ruby 코드의 개발과 리뷰에 적합","코드의 형식화와 최적화를 지원"],"es":["Aplicación de la guía de estilo de Ruby","Mejora de la consistencia y legibilidad del código","Integración con herramientas como RuboCop","Guía para la estructura del código fuente","Principios para la escritura de código legible"],"fr":["Application du guide de style Ruby","Amélioration de la cohérence et de la lisibilité du code","Intégration avec des outils comme RuboCop","Guide pour la structure du code source","Principes pour l''écriture de code lisible"],"de":["Anwendung des Ruby-Style-Leitfadens","Verbesserung der Konsistenz und Lesbarkeit des Codes","Integration mit Tools wie RuboCop","Leitfaden für die Struktur des Quellcodes","Prinzipien für die Erstellung von lesbarem Code"],"pt":["Aplicação do guia de estilo Ruby para melhorar a consistência do código","Uso do RuboCop para garantir a adesão ao guia de estilo","Melhoria da legibilidade do código com layout de código consistente","Compatibilidade com projetos Ruby existentes","Otimização do código para melhor desempenho"],"ru":["Применение руководства по стилю Ruby для улучшения последовательности кода","Использование RuboCop для обеспечения соблюдения руководства по стилю","Повышение читаемости кода с помощью последовательного макета кода","Совместимость с существующими проектами Ruby","Оптимизация кода для лучшей производительности"],"ar":["تطبيق دليل أسلوب روبي لتحسين الاتساق في الكود","استخدام RuboCop لضمان الالتزام بدليل الأسلوب","تحسين قراءة الكود باستخدام تنسيق كود متسق","توافق مع مشاريع روبي الحالية","تحسين الكود لتحقيق أداء أفضل"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use ruby-style","ruby-style alternative","ruby-style vs rubocop","ruby-style install","ruby-style setup guide","what is ruby-style","ruby style guide","rubocop standards","ruby code consistency"],"zh":["Ruby 风格指南","RuboCop","Ruby Style Guide","代码可读性","代码一致性","AIエージェント工具","Ruby 开发","Ruby 代码审查"],"ja":["Ruby スタイルガイド","RuboCop","Ruby Style Guide","コードの可読性","コードの一致性","AIエージェント","Ruby 開発","Ruby コードのレビュー"],"ko":["Ruby 스타일 가이드","RuboCop","Ruby Style Guide","코드의 가독성","코드의 일관성","AI 에이전트","Ruby 개발","Ruby 코드의 리뷰"],"es":["estilo de Ruby","guía de estilo de Ruby","RuboCop","código legible","consistencia del código","herramientas de desarrollo de Ruby","mejora del código","guias de estilo para programadores"],"fr":["style Ruby","guide de style Ruby","RuboCop","code lisible","cohérence du code","outils de développement Ruby","amélioration du code","guides de style pour les programmeurs"],"de":["Ruby-Style-Leitfaden","Stilguide für Ruby","RuboCop","lesbarer Code","Konsistenz des Codes","Entwicklungstools für Ruby","Code-Optimierung","Stilguides für Entwickler"],"pt":["guia de estilo ruby","melhores práticas ruby","desenvolvimento ruby","rubocop","legibilidade de código","consistência de código","otimização de código"],"ru":["руководство по стилю ruby","лучшие практики ruby","разработка ruby","rubocop","читаемость кода","последовательность кода","оптимизация кода"],"ar":["دليل أسلوب روبي","أفضل ممارسات روبي","تطوير روبي","rubocop","قراءة الكود","اتساق الكود","تحسين الكود"]}},"owner":"shubhamtaywade82","repo":"repocontext","repoPath":"shubhamtaywade82/repocontext","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ruby-style","description":"Ruby Style Guide (rubystyle.guide) conventions. Use when writing, formatting, or reviewing Ruby code for layout, naming, flow of control, methods, classes, and idioms. Complements RuboCop.","bodyPreview":"# Ruby Style Guide\n\nThis skill applies the [Ruby Style Guide](https://rubystyle.guide/) — the community style guide that [RuboCop](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop) is based on. Use when writing or reviewing Ruby for consistency and readability.\n\n## Guiding principle\n\n> \"Programs must be written for people to read, and only incidentally for machines to execute.\"\n\nConsistency within a project matters more than strict adherence; when in doubt, match surrounding code.\n\n---\n\n## Source code layout","body":"# Ruby Style Guide\n\nThis skill applies the [Ruby Style Guide](https://rubystyle.guide/) — the community style guide that [RuboCop](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop) is based on. Use when writing or reviewing Ruby for consistency and readability.\n\n## Guiding principle\n\n> \"Programs must be written for people to read, and only incidentally for machines to execute.\"\n\nConsistency within a project matters more than strict adherence; when in doubt, match surrounding code.\n\n---\n\n## Source code layout\n\n- **Encoding:** UTF-8.\n- **Indentation:** Two spaces (no hard tabs).\n- **Line length:** Prefer 80 characters; teams may use up to 120.\n- **No trailing whitespace.** End files with a newline.\n- **No `;`** to terminate statements.\n- **One expression per line** (except e.g. `puts ''a'', ''b''`).\n- **Spaces around operators** (e.g. `sum = 1 + 2`). No space after `!`, inside range literals (`1..3`), or after `{`/before `}` in interpolations.\n- **Safe navigation:** Avoid long `&.` chains; prefer explicit checks or delegation.\n- **Empty lines:** One between method definitions; one around `private`/`protected`; none around method/class/module bodies.\n- **Multi-line method chains:** Use leading `.` or trailing `.` consistently (leading `.` preferred: continue on next line with `.method`).\n- **Method args alignment:** Align multi-line arguments or use single indent; be consistent.\n\n---\n\n## Naming\n\n- **Identifiers in English.** `snake_case` for symbols, methods, variables. `CapitalCase` for classes and modules (e.g. `SomeClass`, `SomeXML`). `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for other constants.\n- **Files and directories:** `snake_case` (e.g. `hello_world.rb`). One class per file; filename mirrors class name.\n- **Predicate methods:** end with `?` (e.g. `empty?`). Avoid prefixing with `is_`, `does_`, `can_`.\n- **Dangerous methods:** end with `!` only when a \"safe\" counterpart exists (e.g. `update!` vs `update`).\n- **Unused variables:** prefix with `_` (e.g. `_unused_var`, or `|_k, v|` in blocks).\n\n---\n\n## Flow of control\n\n- **Prefer iterators over `for`.** Use `each` etc., not `for elem in arr`.\n- **No `then`** for multi-line `if`/`unless`/`when`.\n- **Prefer ternary** for simple branches: `result = condition ? a : b`. Avoid nested ternaries; use `if/else`.\n- **Prefer `case` over `if/elsif`** when comparing the same value. Indent `when` as deep as `case` (outdented).\n- **Use `!` instead of `not`.** Avoid double negation `!!` unless you need an explicit boolean.\n- **Use `&&`/`||` in conditions.** Reserve `and`/`or` for control flow (e.g. `raise or return`) if at all.\n- **Prefer modifier form** for single-line: `do_something if condition`. Avoid modifier at end of long blocks.\n- **Prefer `unless` over `if !`.** Don''t use `else` with `unless`; rewrite with positive case first.\n- **No parentheses** around condition of `if`/`while`/`unless`.\n- **Prefer `loop do` with `break`** over `while true` or `begin...end while`.\n- **Avoid explicit `return`** where the last expression is the return value.\n- **Avoid explicit `self`** except for writers (`self.foo =`), reserved-word method names, or overloaded operators.\n- **Guard clauses:** Prefer early return/`next` over deep nesting. Use guard clauses to bail on invalid input.\n\n---\n\n## Exceptions\n\n- **Prefer `raise` over `fail`.** Use two-arg form: `raise SomeException, ''message''`. Don''t specify `RuntimeError` explicitly in two-arg `raise`.\n- **Don''t return from `ensure`.** Use implicit `begin` (rescue in method). Don''t suppress exceptions; handle or re-raise. Don''t use exceptions for flow of control.\n- **Rescue specific exceptions** (e.g. `StandardError`, `IOError`), not bare `Exception`. Put more specific rescues first.\n\n---\n\n## Methods\n\n- **Keep methods short** (e.g. under 10 LOC). Prefer keyword arguments over long option hashes or many positional args.\n- **Optional/boolean args:** Put required params first; use keyword args for optional/boolean (e.g. `def foo(bar:, baz: false)`).\n- **Omit parentheses** for `def` with no params; use them when there are params. Omit for method calls with no args and for \"keyword\" methods (e.g. `puts`, `raise`) per project convention.\n- **Use `...` for argument forwarding** when delegating (Ruby 2.7+). Use `&` for block forwarding (Ruby 3.1+).\n\n---\n\n## Classes and modules\n\n- **Consistent structure:** extend/include/prepend, inner classes, constants, attr macros, other macros, `def self.`, `initialize`, public methods, then `protected`/`private`.\n- **One mixin per line:** `include Foo` and `include Bar`, not `include Foo, Bar`.\n- **Prefer modules with `module_function`** for namespaces of class methods over classes with only `self.` methods.\n- **Duck typing:** Prefer interfaces (duck typing) over inheritance. No class variables (`@@`); use class instance variables or dependency injection.\n- **Access modifiers:** Use `private`/`protected`; indent them like method definitions with one blank line above and below.\n- **Define `to_s`** for domain objects. Use `attr_reader`/`attr_accessor`; avoid `attr`. Prefer `Struct.new` or `Data.define` for simple value holders (don''t extend them).\n- **Liskov and SOLID:** Subtypes must be substitutable; keep classes SOLID.\n\n---\n\n## Comments and annotations\n\n- **Prefer self-documenting code.** Comment only when explaining *why*. Use English. One space after `#`. Capitalize and punctuate full sentences.\n- **Annotations:** Place above the relevant line. Format as `KEYWORD: note` (e.g. `TODO:`, `FIXME:`, `OPTIMIZE:`, `HACK:`, `REVIEW:`).\n\n---\n\n## Collections and strings\n\n- **Use `[]` and `{}`** for literals. Prefer `%w[]`/`%i[]` for word/symbol arrays. Prefer `key:` over `:key =>` in hashes.\n- **Use `Hash#key?`/`value?`** not `has_key?`/`has_value?`. Use `fetch` for required keys; use block form for expensive defaults.\n- **Prefer `map`/`find`/`select`/`reduce`/`include?`/`size`** over `collect`/`detect`/`find_all`/`inject`/`member?`/`length` where it helps readability.\n- **Use `any?`/`none?`/`one?`** instead of `count > 0` etc. Don''t use `count` when `size`/`length` is enough (e.g. for Hash).\n- **Strings:** Prefer interpolation: `\"#{a} #{b}\"`. Use single quotes when no interpolation/special chars. Use `<<` for building large strings. Use `\\A` and `\\z` for full-string regex (not `^`/`$`).\n\n---\n\n## Other\n\n- **Use `require_relative`** for internal code; `require` for external libs. Omit `.rb` in `require`/`require_relative`.\n- **Prefer `predicate?` and `Comparable#between?`** over manual comparisons where it clarifies intent.\n- **Don''t mutate params** unless that''s the method''s purpose. Avoid more than ~3 levels of block nesting.\n- **Prefer `public_send`** over `send`; prefer `__send__` if the name might be overridden.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n- [Ruby Style Guide](https://rubystyle.guide/) — full guide\n- [RuboCop](https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop) — linter and formatter based on this guide\n- [RSpec Style Guide](https://github.com/rubocop/rspec-style-guide) — complementary guide\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:09:51.888Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing consistent Ruby coding standards and readability","zh":"非常适合需要一致的Ruby编码标准和可读性的代码审查代理","ja":"Rubyのコードの標準化と可読性が必要なコードレビューエージェントに適しています","ko":"일관된 Ruby 코딩 표준과 가독성이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan estándares de codificación de Ruby consistentes y legibilidad","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Révision de Code ayant besoin de normes de codage Ruby cohérentes et de lisibilité","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die konsistente Ruby-Codierungsstandards und Lesbarkeit benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de padrões de codificação Ruby consistentes e legibilidade","ru":"Идеально для агентов рассмотрения кода, которым необходимы последовательные стандарты кодирования Ruby и читаемость","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المراجعة الكود التي تحتاج إلى معايير برمجة روبي ثابتة وقابلية القراءة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce the Ruby Style Guide, utilizing RuboCop for consistent source code layout and style, ensuring readability and maintainability of Ruby projects through guidelines and community-driven standards","zh":"赋予代理人执行Ruby风格指南的能力，利用RuboCop实现一致的源代码布局和风格，通过指南和社区驱动的标准确保Ruby项目的可读性和可维护性","ja":"Ruby Style Guideを実施するエージェントを可能にし、RuboCopを使用して一貫したソースコードのレイアウトとスタイルを実現し、ガイドラインとコミュニティ主導の標準を通じてRubyプロジェクトの可読性とメンテナンス性を確保する","ko":"에이전트가 Ruby 스타일 가이드를 시행할 수 있도록 하는데, RuboCop를 사용하여 일관된 소스 코드 레이아웃과 스타일을 구현하여 가이드라인과 커뮤니티 주도 표준을 통하여 Ruby 프로젝트의 가독성과 유지 보수성을 보장합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar la Guía de Estilo de Ruby, utilizando RuboCop para un diseño y estilo de código fuente coherentes, garantizando la legibilidad y mantenibilidad de los proyectos Ruby a través de directrices y estándares impulsados por la comunidad","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer le Guide de Style Ruby, en utilisant RuboCop pour une mise en page et un style de code source cohérents, garantissant la lisibilité et la maintenabilité des projets Ruby grâce à des directives et des normes impulsées par la communauté","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, den Ruby-Stilführer durchzusetzen, indem RuboCop für eine konsistente Quellcode-Layout und -Stil verwendet wird, um die Lesbarkeit und Wartbarkeit von Ruby-Projekten durch Richtlinien und communitygetriebene Standards sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita agentes a impor o Guia de Estilo Ruby, utilizando RuboCop para layout e estilo de código-fonte consistentes, garantindo legibilidade e manutenibilidade de projetos Ruby por meio de diretrizes e padrões impulsionados pela comunidade","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить соблюдение Руководства по стилю Ruby, используя RuboCop для последовательного макета и стиля исходного кода, обеспечивая читаемость и поддерживаемость проектов Ruby посредством руководящих принципов и стандартов, определяемых сообществом","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء قدرة على فرض دليل أسلوب روبي، باستخدام RuboCop من أجل تخطيط ونمط شفرة مصدر متسق، ضمان سهولة القراءة وضمان استدامة مشاريع روبي من خلال إرشادات ومعايير مدفوعة بالمجتمع"},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing Ruby Style Guide for consistent coding","Improving code readability through standardized layout","Automating code reviews for Ruby projects"],"zh":["执行一致的Ruby编码标准","通过标准化布局改进代码可读性","自动化Ruby项目的代码审查"],"ja":["一貫したRubyコードのスタイルを実施する","標準化されたレイアウトを通じてコードの可読性を向上させる","Rubyプロジェクトのコードレビューを自動化する"],"ko":["일관된 Ruby 코딩 표준 시행","표준화된 레이아웃을 통해 코드 가독성 향상","Ruby 프로젝트의 코드 리뷰 자동화"],"es":["Aplicar la Guía de Estilo de Ruby para una codificación coherente","Mejorar la legibilidad del código a través de un diseño estandarizado","Automatizar las revisiones de código para proyectos Ruby"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre le Guide de Style Ruby pour une codification cohérente","Améliorer la lisibilité du code grâce à une mise en page standardisée","Automatiser les révisions de code pour les projets Ruby"],"de":["Durchsetzen des Ruby-Stilführers für eine konsistente Kodierung","Verbesserung der Lesbarkeit des Codes durch ein standardisiertes Layout","Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für Ruby-Projekte"],"pt":["Impor Guia de Estilo Ruby para codificação consistente","Melhorar legibilidade do código por meio de layout padronizado","Automatizar revisões de código para projetos Ruby"],"ru":["Обеспечение соблюдения Руководства по стилю Ruby для последовательного кодирования","Улучшение читаемости кода за счет стандартизированного макета","Автоматизация рассмотрения кода для проектов Ruby"],"ar":["فرض دليل أسلوب روبي من أجل الترميز الثابت","تحسين قراءة الشفرة من خلال تخطيط معياري","تأتمة مراجعة الشفرة لمشاريع روبي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Ruby environment","Limited to Ruby projects","Adherence to community style guide may vary based on project specifics"],"zh":["需要Ruby环境","仅限Ruby项目","遵守社区风格指南可能会根据项目具体情况有所不同"],"ja":["Ruby環境が必要","Rubyプロジェクトのみ","コミュニティのスタイルガイドへの準拠はプロジェクトの具体的な状況によって異なる場合がある"],"ko":["Ruby 환경 필요","Ruby 프로젝트만 해당","커뮤니티 스타일 가이드 준수는 프로젝트의 구체적인 상황에 따라 다를 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere un entorno Ruby","Limitado a proyectos Ruby","La adherencia a la guía de estilo de la comunidad puede variar en función de las especificaciones del proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Ruby","Limité aux projets Ruby","Le respect du guide de style de la communauté peut varier en fonction des spécificités du projet"],"de":["Benötigt eine Ruby-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Ruby-Projekte","Die Einhaltung des communitygetriebenen Stilführers kann je nach Projektspezifika variieren"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Ruby","Limitado a projetos Ruby","A adesão ao guia de estilo da comunidade pode variar com base em especificidades do projeto"],"ru":["Требуется среда Ruby","Ограничен для проектов Ruby","Соблюдение руководства по стилю сообщества может варьироваться в зависимости от конкретики проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة روبي","محدود لمشاريع روبي","الامتثال لدليل أسلوب المجتمع قد يختلف بناءً على تفاصيل المشروع"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"f5067ec388dbdacc7a4584057eabcba5717ce9635d0b26634df47f2ff8cbb86c","qualityScore":26}');
